&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Candidate Profile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The strongest candidates meet most of the following.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Experience as a Personal Assistant or Executive Assistant, ideally supporting senior leaders in the Zurich area. You know how the job works: you take a quick handover and run with it, without needing detailed instructions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education: &lt;/strong&gt;A commercial apprenticeship (KV), a degree from a university of applied sciences, or comparable training. A university degree is not required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Anticipation &amp;amp; Ownership: &lt;/strong&gt;You see what needs doing and handle it without being asked. When the situation is unclear and nobody is around to ask, you make a good decision on your own.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pace &amp;amp; Attitude: &lt;/strong&gt;Quick, organised and hands-on. You take pride in getting the details right.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial Understanding: &lt;/strong&gt;Comfortable with numbers and invoices. Experience with billing or project accounting is a plus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People: &lt;/strong&gt;Warm and approachable with colleagues, candidates and clients alike.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Discretion: &lt;/strong&gt;You handle confidential information, such as candidate data, client details and financials, with care.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Languages: &lt;/strong&gt;Fluency in German and English, written and spoken, is required. Swiss German is a strong plus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Eligibility: &lt;/strong&gt;You must be eligible to work in Switzerland.&lt;/p&gt;
