&lt;p&gt;Artefact is a next-generation data and AI consulting firm dedicated to accelerating the adoption of data and AI to create measurable business impact across the full enterprise value chain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We sit at the intersection of consulting, data science, AI technologies, data engineering, and digital transformation. We do not just advise — we build, implement, and deliver results our clients can measure. Our teams bring together consultants, data scientists, data engineers, AI engineers, analysts, and digital experts to solve complex business challenges with pragmatic, production-ready solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we continue to grow in the US, we are building a team of entrepreneurial data and AI talent who can help clients move beyond experimentation and into scalable, governed, value-generating AI adoption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Artefact is looking for a Senior AI &amp;amp; Data Consultant: an analytical, client-facing consultant who is also a hands-on builder with AI.&amp;nbsp;You will perform advanced analytics, interface directly with clients, and keep project efforts aligned and on track — and you will do it AI-natively. Our senior consultants use AI tools to analyze faster, write better, and prototype what they recommend. When the team needs a quick proof of concept, you&#39;re the one who opens Claude Code or Gemini CLI and builds it. We need someone who is not afraid of the terminal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define client needs through interviews with client teams and technology partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform advanced data analysis and research on high-impact, strategic client problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build, formulate, and present strategic data and AI recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep internal project efforts aligned and on track, and interface with clients with confidence and care.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI tools daily across your work: analysis, synthesis, writing, and quality checking — with the judgment to verify outputs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype ideas with agentic coding tools (Claude Code, Gemini CLI, Codex): a working demo, an automated analysis, a small internal tool.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply core GenAI concepts — prompting, RAG, agents, context engineering — well enough to explain them to clients and stress-test vendor claims.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop specialization in at least one AI platform ecosystem: Google (Gemini), Anthropic (Claude), or OpenAI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present insights to clients in clear, compelling language — to technical and non-technical audiences alike.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to new business proposals and to Artefact-published content (research, articles, business cases).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee and mentor entry-level consultants and interns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5 years of full-time work experience, ideally in consulting, data/analytics, marketing, advertising, finance, or tech.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills and experience presenting data-driven recommendations to clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on AI literacy: regular use of AI tools for real work, and demonstrated willingness to build — prototypes, automations, analyses — with AI assistance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with the terminal, and with tools like Claude Code or Gemini CLI (or clear evidence you&#39;ll get there fast).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of SQL and/or Python for data analysis; advanced Excel and PowerPoint/Google Workspace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills, client-facing and intercultural.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A teaching orientation: willingness to mentor junior team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Undergraduate degree, preferably in business, technology, or another field related to our work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
