&lt;h3&gt;About the role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Artefact is growing quickly across the US and Canada, and we’re looking for a Technical Talent Acquisition Partner to help us identify, attract, and hire exceptional talent across consulting and technical disciplines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on recruiting role for someone who can move quickly, source creatively, partner closely with hiring managers, and maintain a high hiring bar in a competitive market. You’ll own searches from intake through offer, build strong candidate pipelines, and help ensure a high-quality experience for both candidates and hiring teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the organization scales, you’ll also be responsible for campus recruiting and contribute to broader talent acquisition initiatives, including talent pipelining, workforce planning, and recruiting process improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full recruitment lifecycle across the US, Canada, and Latin America, leading searches across both consulting and technical functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary Talent Acquisition partner for the region, independently managing the recruiting function across multiple business lines, hiring managers, and competing priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with hiring managers and chapter leads to define hiring strategies, workforce needs, role requirements, and ideal candidate profiles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit across consulting and technical disciplines, including AI, data science, analytics, data engineering, machine learning, and other specialized roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead campus recruiting, including building university partnerships, representing Artefact at career fairs and campus events, and managing the intern and graduate hiring pipeline from sourcing through offer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build proactive, diverse talent pipelines using modern sourcing techniques, direct outreach, referrals, networking, talent communities, market mapping, and AI-powered recruiting tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver an exceptional candidate experience from the initial conversation through onboarding while ensuring a high-quality and efficient hiring process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a trusted advisor to leaders on hiring decisions, interview quality, candidate evaluation, compensation positioning, and talent market trends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance day-to-day recruiting execution with broader talent acquisition initiatives, including employer branding, recruiting operations, interview training, and process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze recruiting metrics to identify trends, forecast hiring outcomes, and recommend data-driven improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and continuously improve scalable recruiting programs, structured interview processes, hiring documentation, workflows, and recruiting best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion an inclusive hiring process grounded in structured assessments, objective decision-making, and consistent evaluation criteria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and strengthen the Artefact employer brand through social media, networking events, community partnerships, and talent marketing initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI and emerging recruiting technologies to streamline sourcing, interview preparation, candidate communications, scheduling, reporting, and recruiting workflows while maintaining ethical and compliant recruiting practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate must have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience within a consulting or professional services environment, with a demonstrated ability to support a fast-paced, high-growth environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong &lt;strong&gt;technical recruiting &lt;/strong&gt;experience across AI, data engineering, analytics, data science, machine learning, and other specialized technical roles, as well as experience recruiting for consulting and client-facing positions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience creating Greenhouse workflows, reporting, and dashboards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success serving as a trusted talent advisor and building strong partnerships with hiring managers, business leaders, and technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to independently manage multiple searches across functions, geographies, and levels while balancing competing priorities in a fast-paced, high-growth environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong sourcing expertise, with a track record of building diverse, high-quality candidate pipelines through direct sourcing, referrals, networking, market mapping, talent communities, and other sourcing strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and improving recruiting processes, structured interview practices, hiring documentation, hiring manager training, and scalable recruiting programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills, with the ability to translate recruiting metrics, pipeline data, and labor market insights into actionable recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using applicant tracking systems, recruiting analytics, sourcing technologies, and AI-enabled recruiting tools to improve efficiency and hiring outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine interest in AI and emerging technologies, with the ability to quickly learn new tools and thoughtfully incorporate them into recruiting workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to establish credibility, influence stakeholders, and build relationships across technical and business teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and project management skills, with the ability to prioritize effectively, navigate ambiguity, and maintain momentum in a rapidly evolving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A high degree of ownership, sound judgment, adaptability, and a proactive, solutions-oriented approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Human Resources, Business, Psychology, Communications, or a related field preferred. Equivalent professional experience will also be considered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why you should join us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are united by our &lt;strong&gt;values&lt;/strong&gt; and strengthened by our hybrid &lt;strong&gt;expertise&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;There is always a way:&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;re from the breed of does, of diggers, of makers. Because ideas are valuable only if executed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client trust is won on the field:&lt;/strong&gt; Addressing client needs flows better hands on at their side.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If not used, it is useless:&lt;/strong&gt; Our love for technology translates into a steep desire for adoption, true brilliance is about impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If not shared, our work is not done:&lt;/strong&gt; Sharing knowledge is the best way to button up a mission, benefitting clients and colleagues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We learn everyday:&lt;/strong&gt; Tech is a land where everything move at the speed of light, you better be ready to challenge yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Support Our People&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to our values-driven culture, we offer a range of benefits and programs designed to support our employees&#39; growth and well-being, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learning and Development: &lt;/strong&gt;Work alongside a multidisciplinary team of AI, data, and consulting experts who are committed to continuous learning, knowledge sharing, and professional growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hybrid Flexibility:&lt;/strong&gt; Our hybrid work model gives you the flexibility to balance collaboration, client needs, and personal commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comprehensive Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt; We offer a competitive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision coverage, a 401(k) plan with company matching, and paid parental leave.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Time to Recharge:&lt;/strong&gt; We believe sustainable performance matters. That&#39;s why we offer unlimited paid time off, giving you the flexibility to take the time you need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth Opportunities:&lt;/strong&gt; As a rapidly growing organization, you&#39;ll have the opportunity to expand your skills, take on new challenges, and help shape the future of the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The estimated base compensation for this role is $100,000 - $125,000 (NYC location). Individual compensation is determined by skills, qualifications, and experience. In addition, this role is eligible for competitive benefits.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
